<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<speak version="1.1" xml:lang="en-US">
  <voice name="en-US-AndrewNeural">
    <prosody rate="+0%" pitch="+0Hz">
      <p id="scene-01">StatePort starts with named applications, not a blank chat. This private-alpha fixture shows ongoing work with its own purpose, durable state, decisions, and history.</p>
      <p id="scene-02">The application plane provides purpose and continuity. StatePort owns intent, authority, canonical state, evidence, and acceptance. Those facts do not belong to an agent session.</p>
      <p id="scene-03">Conversation is one view inside the application. The execution plane is separate: the harness runs an authorized task and returns observations and candidate output, but it does not own accepted state.</p>
      <p id="scene-04">The source view says whether an application source is verified. A development candidate can provide isolated-test evidence, but it does not silently become a canonical release or production install.</p>
      <p id="scene-05">The same application list remains readable on a small screen. This is a local interface view, not evidence of a separate mobile release.</p>
      <p id="scene-06">This private alpha has one exercised provider path: Codex in supervised-direct mode. Other providers are not qualified by this walkthrough, and there is no public software download yet.</p>
    </prosody>
  </voice>
</speak>
